From 045f8515eae3f56790849ab40d2d35b3f075006c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:37:30 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] 034 A2 (TKOffset): no silent invalid thick solid or offset -
 structural guard

Stage A caught broken offsets only where a face can fold. Thick solids
with removed faces tangent to their neighbours (a box filleted on all 12
edges with the top removed, PartDesign Thickness) still came back with
two shells and a face of bad orientation, IsDone() true (issue 034 A2).

Always on, pure topology, linear in the number of edges:
- every shell of a solid of the result is closed and coherently oriented:
  an edge used once, or by two faces in the same direction, is an error
  (the manifold part of BRepCheck_Shell Closed/Orientation, so only
  results BRepCheck rejects can change; Requicha 1980);
- a thick solid has at most one shell per piece of the remaining input
  faces that has a free edge and two per closed piece (the opening joins
  the piece to its offset; Forsyth 1995); more shells = the opening was
  not cut -> error.
Only with the intersection join and a tangent edge of a free-form face
(ill-conditioned intersection of tangent offsets) is the result checked
like a folding one (BRepCheck + BOP self-interference).

Failure: IsDone() false, UnknownError (structure) or CannotTrimEdges
(check). No header, member, export or import change (exports 480 =
weekly, import set = stage A).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
